       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day for adults. Higher doses carry more risk of significant hypotension, peripheral edema, and reflex tachycardia. They usually add little extra blood-pressure control.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** This is an intentional supra-maximal dose. If you choose this, I'll add a note to the order documenting that it was intended, and I'd suggest a rationale and monitoring plan.\n3. **Add a second agent instead**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, if the goal is more BP control. Tell me the drug and dose and I'll enter it.\n\nI can enter whichever you choose as soon as you confirm."
      }
